.TH POPULATIONMODEL 2
.SH NAME
Populationmodel \- common interface for live compartment and population models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "danby/populationmodel.m";
modelmodule: Populationmodel;

modelmodule = load Populationmodel path;
model := modelmodule->new();
modelmodule->evaluate(model,t,state,derivative);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Populationmodel
is the structural interface used by independent Danby equation modules with
an arbitrary number of nonnegative state quantities.  It separates equations
and model metadata from integration, plotting, window management, and input.
.PP
Each implementation exports a constructor, a title, state and parameter
labels, parameter display ranges, and an evaluation function.  The returned
.B Model
contains mutable parameter values and the default initial state.  Implementors
define the ADT's
.B rhs
method and expose it through
.B evaluate
so clients need not import colliding ADT method names from several models.
.SH INTERFACE
.TP
.B new()
Return a fresh model instance.  Arrays must not be shared between calls.
.TP
.B statelabels()
Return one concise display label for every element of
.BR Model.initial .
.TP
.B parameterlabels(), parameterranges()
Return parallel arrays matching
.BR Model.parameter .
Every range is the positive upper endpoint used by direct-manipulation tracks.
.TP
.B evaluate(model,t,state,derivative)
Evaluate the right-hand side without advancing time.  State and derivative
must have the same length as
.BR Model.initial .
.SH CLIENT
.B /dis/temple/populations.dis
is the reusable live client.  It constructs a named Plot table, integrates
with
.IR numerics (2),
draws one history per state, and supplies directly editable current-state bars
and parameter tracks.  A public application normally wraps it with the model
path and manual-page stem rather than duplicating the client.
.SH FILES
.B /module/danby/populationmodel.m
.br
.B /appl/temple/populations.b
.br
.B /dis/temple/populations.dis
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2),
.IR plot (2)
